{"id": "swebq0077", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 4.22, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2233, "eot_read_ms": 25, "reference_answer": "Presidential system;Federal republic;Representative democracy;Two-party system;Constitutional republic;Republic", "query": "what type of government does the us constitution set up?", "transcript": "What type of government does the US Constitution set up?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The US Constitution sets up a federal system of government. It creates three branches of government the legislative branch which makes laws, the executive branch which carries out laws, and the judicial branch which interprets laws. The government is also divided between the national government and state governments so power is shared.", "answer_ms": 1589}
