{"id": "swebq0104", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.18, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3064, "eot_read_ms": 25, "reference_answer": "Padua", "query": "what is st anthony patron saint of?", "transcript": "Who is Saint Anthony patron saint of?", "mode": "local", "answer": "St. Anthony is the patron saint of many things, but he's especially known as the patron saint of lost things. People often turn to him when they've misplaced something important. He's also the patron saint of hope, because even when things seem lost, he reminds us that there's always a chance for finding what we need.", "answer_ms": 1936}
