{"id": "swebq0116", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.51, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2622, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "william averell harriman appointed by john fitzgerald kennedy", "query": "who did john kennedy have affairs with?", "transcript": "Who did John Kennedy have affairs with?", "mode": "local", "answer": "John F. Kennedy, the 35th President of the United States, had several extramarital affairs during his life. One of the most well-known was with Judith Campbell Exner, whom he met in Cuba and with whom he maintained a relationship for years. Another significant affair was with Mary Pinchot Meyer, a socialite who later became involved with other high-profile figures as well. These relationships were part of Kennedy's private life and have been subjects of historical interest and speculation.", "answer_ms": 3300}
{"id": "swebq0119", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.6, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2653, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "Semi-presidential system;Republic;Unitary state", "query": "what system of government does guyana have?", "transcript": "What system of government does Guyana have?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Guyana is a parliamentary representative democratic republic. That means the country has a president as the head of state and a prime minister as the head of government. The president is elected by popular vote for a five-year term, while the prime minister is chosen by the National Assembly, usually the leader of the majority party or coalition. The legislative power is held by the National Assembly, which is made up of 65 members elected through general elections. So overall, Guyana operates under a system where the people elect representatives who then form the government, with both executive and legislative branches working together to run the country.", "answer_ms": 3925}
{"id": "swebq0122", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.51, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2315, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "Scotland", "query": "what countries does england border?", "transcript": "Which countries does England border?", "mode": "local", "answer": "England is bordered by Scotland to the north, Wales to the west, and the sea on all other sides. So it borders one country—Scotland—and is surrounded by the North Sea to the east, the Irish Sea to the west, and the English Channel to the south.", "answer_ms": 1707}
{"id": "swebq0125", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.18, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3145, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "William Penn", "query": "where does name pennsylvania come from?", "transcript": "Where does name Pennsylvania come from?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Pennsylvania is named after William Penn. He was a man who loved peace and helping people. A very important king, Charles II, gave this land to William Penn as a gift. So, the place became known as Pennsylvania, which means \"Penn's Woods.\" It's like saying, \"This beautiful area belongs to Penn!\" Isn't that a nice story?", "answer_ms": 2244}
