{"id": "swebq0131", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.04, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1958, "eot_read_ms": 26, "reference_answer": "Mathematician;Physicist;Philosopher;Astronomer;Scientist;Chemist", "query": "who was isaac newton and what did he do?", "transcript": "Who was Isaac Newton and what did he do?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Isaac Newton was an English scientist and mathematician. He lived in the late 1600s and early 1700s. Newton is famous for his work in physics, mathematics, and astronomy. He helped explain how things move, like apples falling from trees or planets going around the sun. One of his most important ideas is that everything in the universe pulls on everything else with a force called gravity. He also discovered how white light can be broken into many colors when it passes through a prism. Because of these discoveries, Newton changed the way people understand the world and space.", "answer_ms": 3396}
{"id": "swebq0134", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 3.95, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2385, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "Google Maps;Google Calendar;Google SketchUp;Google Docs and Spreadsheets;Blogger;Picasa;Google Talk;Google X;Gmail", "query": "what products and\\/or services does google offer customers?", "transcript": "What products and or services does Google offer customers?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Google offers a wide range of products and services to its customers, including the following key offerings:\\n\\n1. **Search Engine**: Google Search is one of the most widely used search engines for finding information on the web.\\n2. **Advertising**: Google Ads allows businesses to create and display ads across the Google network and partner websites.\\n3. **Android**: A mobile operating system that powers smartphones, tablets, and other devices.\\n4. **Gmail**: A free email service with robust features like spam filtering and integration with other Google services.\\n5. **Google Workspace**:\\n   - **Gmail**, \\n   - **Google Drive** for cloud storage,\\n   - **Google Docs**, Sheets, and Slides for collaborative document creation,\\n   - **Google Meet** for video conferencing.\\n6. **YouTube**: A video-sharing platform where users can upload, view, and share videos.\\n7. **Google Maps**: A mapping service providing directions, location data, and street views.\\n8. **Google Assistant**: An AI-powered virtual assistant available on various devices for voice-activated help.\\n9. **Chrome Browser**: A popular web browser known for speed and security.\\n10. **Play Store**: A digital distribution platform for Android apps, games, music, books, and more.\\n\\nThese products and services are designed to meet the diverse needs of individuals, businesses, and organizations worldwide.", "answer_ms": 10357}
